# What must never enter the image.
#
# .env.local holds the database URL, the Anthropic key and the connection secret. An image is not a
# private thing — it is pushed to a registry, pulled, and its layers are readable by anyone holding
# it. Secrets belong in the environment at run time, never baked into a layer.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Rebuilt inside the image, and copying a host build in would defeat the point of building one.
node_modules
dist

# Data and history, not source.
generated-projects
.git
.attic
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not build inputs. Note what is *not* listed: src/, index.html, vite.config.* and tsconfig*.json all
# have to reach the build stage or `npm run build` has nothing to compile. They stop there — the
# runtime stage copies only server/ and the finished dist/, so none of them ends up in the image.
docs
.github
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
